{{/*
Shared fragments of the generated GitHub Actions workflows.

privateModulesAccess renders the pair of job steps that let a job fetch Go
modules that are not served by the module proxy: the credential rewrite that
makes git send the token to github.com, and GOPRIVATE, which is what sends
those fetches to git in the first place.

The two steps are one block on purpose. GOPRIVATE is what takes a module off
proxy.golang.org and onto a direct git fetch — which is exactly the fetch the
credential rewrite serves. Setting one without the other is never what a job
wants, so there is nothing to render separately.

The block renders only when the project declares private modules
(git.private_repos, read here through .GoPrivate so that every consumer of the
value agrees — see GeneratorParams.GoPrivate). Without them the proxy serves
every dependency, so there is nothing to take off it and no token to need. The
condition lives here rather than at each call site, so that the whole question
is one `if` and not one per workflow job.

Call it with the root context ($): the goat-tests jobs are rendered inside a
range over the applications, where "." is one application and the fragment
would render empty.

The body deliberately starts with two newlines and ends without one, so that a
call on a line of its own renders the block separated from the step above by a
blank line, as the steps of these workflows are, and renders nothing at all —
not even a stray blank line — when there is nothing to render. The first
newline is what terminates the line above, so the call must be left-trimmed
("{{- template" and not "{{ template"); the define tag must not be trimmed on
the right ("-}}"), as that would eat both newlines and the indentation of the
first step, which YAML needs.
*/}}
{{- define "privateModulesAccess" }}{{ if .GoPrivate }}

      - name: Configure Git for private repos
        env:
          GH_TOKEN: ${{"{{"}} secrets.{{ .PrivateReposTokenSecretName }} {{"}}"}}
        run: |
          git config --global url."https://x-access-token:${GH_TOKEN}@github.com/".insteadOf "https://github.com/"

      - name: Set GOPRIVATE
        run: |
          go env -w GOPRIVATE="{{ .GoPrivate }}"
{{- end }}{{ end }}
